WF-44 — Feedback Recorder

## Summary

- Purpose: Pure recorder. Its sole caller, WF-43, calls it ONLY after WF-25 has already classified the message as `feedback_intent` and already routed rebook/stop elsewhere — so WF-44 just saves the feedback and acknowledges. It does not re-classify.
- Inputs (WF-01 canonical envelope §2.1, forwarded by WF-43): `phoneNumber` (top-level), `messageContent` (the feedback text), `user.{id, status}`.
- Outputs: feedback text saved to the `users` row; a WhatsApp acknowledgement.
- State Transitions: none on the user lifecycle status (clears `stage` to NULL).
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-50 (Send WhatsApp).
- Called by: WF-43 (post-feedback_intent) — sole caller (confirmed across all live workflows 2026-05-29).
- **Deltas vs the prior WF-44 (safety-net §6, decision #11):**
  - REMOVED the `Call WF-25` node and the `rebook_intent?` → WF-45 / `stop_intent?` → WF-47 re-route branches. WF-43 already classified + routed those before calling WF-44, so the re-classify was dead redundancy — and post-redesign it would double-count the safety-net threshold.
  - WF-44 no longer calls WF-25, WF-45, or WF-47. No Gemini call.
- **Notes:**
  - Copy reuse-existing — verify verbatim at build.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — triggered by WF-43 after the message was classified `feedback_intent`. Read `phoneNumber`, `messageContent`, `user.id` from the envelope.
Step 2: UPDATE chinmay_astro.users SET feedback = messageContent, stage = NULL, updated_at = NOW() WHERE id = user.id.
Step 3: Send the acknowledgement — call WF-50 with `{ phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', messageContent: "🙏 Thank you for your feedback! We really appreciate you taking the time to share your experience with Chinmay's consultation service. Your input helps us improve." }`. End.
